cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "LR-DSR: latent-regime clustering by symbolic law"
abstract: >-
  Each window of data came from one of K unknown closed-form laws; LR-DSR
  recovers which law produced each window and writes each law as a formula,
  by alternating a symbolic fit per regime with a reassignment of every
  window, started in a space of law coefficients. With the theory of the
  best possible error, a problem zoo, real data, and a tutorial.
authors:
  - family-names: Jacoby
    given-names: Dror
    affiliation: Tel Aviv University
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/drorjac/lrdsr-clustering"
date-released: 2026-09-29
keywords:
  - symbolic regression
  - clustering
  - latent regimes
  - mixture of regressions
  - time series
